DESCRIPTION:Pocky Day\, known in Japan as Pocky & Pretz Day\, falls on Nove
 mber 11 because the date written 11/11 looks like a row of the chocolate-c
 oated biscuit sticks it celebrates. Ezaki Glico\, which makes them\, estab
 lished the day in 1999 and had it certified as an official anniversary. Th
 at makes it one of the rare food holidays whose origin is documented\, bec
 ause the company that invented the snack also invented the day.\n\nhttps:/
